  "steps": [
    "Bring a large pot of salted water to a rolling boil over high heat. Add the chickpea pasta and cook uncovered for 7 to 9 minutes, stirring occasionally, until al dente. Drain thoroughly and set aside.",
    "In a large bowl, combine the ground turkey, breadcrumbs, egg, parmesan cheese, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper. Mix gently with your hands just until incorporated, then shape the mixture into 16 equal-sized meatballs.",
    "Heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 2 minutes until shimmering. Add the turkey meatballs in a single layer and sear for 5 minutes, turning occasionally, until golden brown on all sides.",
    "Pour the marinara sauce directly over the browned meatballs in the skillet. Reduce the heat to medium-low, cover with a lid, and simmer for 8 to 10 minutes until the meatballs reach an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C) and the sauce is bubbling.",
    "Divide the cooked chickpea pasta among four bowls, top generously with the turkey meatballs and marinara sauce, and garnish with additional parmesan cheese before serving."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Do not overmix the turkey meatball mixture or the meatballs will turn out dense rather than tender.",
    "Chickpea pasta cooks quickly and can foam up; stir it frequently during the boil.",
    "Store leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Reheat gently on the stovetop or in the microwave.",
